* CPMDIR - CP/M 3 DIRECTORY LISTING

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* CPMDIR - CP/M 3 DIRECTORY LISTING

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:CPMDIR [filespec] [options]

Lists files using the original CP/M 3 directory program. Example:
SYSUTLS:CPMDIR I14:*.HLP

Options use square brackets, for example [FULL] for detailed information
or [SYS] for system files. This utility differs from public DIR, which is
the supplied directory front end. It does not change caller access policy.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
